<title>BELGIUM: W. Europe car registrations up 12.2 pct in Sept.</title>
<headline>W. Europe car registrations up 12.2 pct in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are provisional West European new car registrations and market share figures for September released on Monday by the European Automobile Manufacturers Association (ACEA).</p>
<p> Brand		   Sept 96    pct change  mkt share vs Sept 95</p>
<p>							   (pct)	 (pct)</p>
<p> All brands	     971,600   +12.2</p>
<p> Volkswagen	     171,500   +12.9	   17.7	 17.5</p>
<p> PSA			128,241   +29.1	   13.2	 11.5</p>
<p> GM			 116,984   +11.2	   12.0	 12.2</p>
<p> Renault		  106,380   +34.5	   10.9	  9.1</p>
<p> Japanese		 104,658    +6.8	   10.8	 11.3</p>
<p> Ford		     102,030    -0.7	   10.5	 11.9</p>
<p> Fiat			99,800    +3.9	   10.3	 11.1</p>
<p> BMW			 56,655    +2.3	    5.8	  6.4</p>
<p> Mercedes		  36,600   +18.3	    3.8	  3.6</p>
<p> Korean		    21,014   +28.5	    2.2	  1.9</p>
<p> Volvo		     19,088    -4.9	    2.0	  2.3</p>
<p>(Volkswagen includes Audi, Seat, Skoda. GM includes Opel/Vauxhall, U.S. imports, Saab, IBC/ISUZU. Ford includes U.S. imports, Jaguar. Fiat includes Lancia, Alfa Romeo, Innocenti, Ferrari, Maserati. PSA includes Peugeot, Citroen. Japanese includes Nissan, Toyota, Mazda, Honda, Mitsubishi, others. BMW includes Rover. ACEA provides no breakdown for the Korean figures.)</p>
</text>
